**How to implement.** The uniaxial crystal builder becomes product physics on its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16: reusable tensor construction lives on product parameter records while the required ground-truth/design builders retain their test-support home; the S10.1 brief 'UniaxialParameters gets the uniaxial builder MuellerInverseTests uses'). Two copies exist today, `buildUniaxialGyrotropic` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:buildUniaxialGyrotropic`) and its body-for-body duplicates `buildLangasite` (`LangasiteInverseTests.fs:buildLangasite`) and the fact-local `buildUniaxial` of `BiaxialInverseTests`' `the triclinic parameter set is a strict generalization of the uniaxial one` (`BiaxialInverseTests.fs:433`); all three go (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs`, `UniaxialParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:UniaxialParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is the deleted builder's: `OpticalProperties.type_3_4_6_Crystal (EpsValue.fromRefractionIndex this.ordinaryIndex) (EpsValue.fromRefractionIndex this.extraordinaryIndex) this.g11 this.g33`, so diag(n_o², n_o², n_e²) and diag(g₁₁, g₁₁, g₃₃) stay the engine's own (`OpticalProperties/Active.fs:type_3_4_6_Crystal`). Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of a uniaxial gyrotropic crystal (classes 3/32/4/422/6/622) with these four constants, through the engine's class 3/4/6 builder (spec 0050 §3.16). `MuellerInverse.fs` opens `OpticalProperties.Active`, which Domain already reaches through its `Analytics` reference (`MaterialLibrary.fs:12` opens it). The module doc's sentence that `OpticalConstructor.Domain` does not reference `OpticalProperties`, so that nothing here names a crystal class (`MuellerInverse.fs:15-20`), becomes: the forward proxy takes a caller-supplied `'Parameters -> OpticalProperties` builder, each parameter record carries its crystal class's builder as `opticalProperties` (spec 0050 §3.16), and no named material lives here. No other line of the file changes. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`: delete `buildUniaxialGyrotropic` with its doc; `forward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`; in `orientForCut carries the optic axis from the surface normal into the surface plane` `props` is `quartz.opticalProperties`. (3) `Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs`: delete `buildLangasite` with its doc; `forward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs`: in `the triclinic parameter set is a strict generalization of the uniaxial one`, delete the local `buildUniaxial`; `uniaxialForward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member evaluates the same expression the three builders did. No test is added or removed. `LangasiteInverseTests`, whose facts drive the uniaxial member through `forward`, is the cheapest class that exercises it.

**Acceptance.** After the promotion, `UniaxialParameters.opticalProperties` MUST be the one uniaxial builder, `buildUniaxialGyrotropic`, `buildLangasite` and `BiaxialInverseTests`' local `buildUniaxial` MUST be gone, and the three uniaxial forward models MUST read the member; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.
